{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNy4nJGxjPowiau9Us8O","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking whether the Figma Plugin API supports creating instances of existing components across pages and, more broadly, wants a plan for building the ABM developer portfolio. The answer is yes: `component.createInstance()` works across pages, so I build in \"03 · Workspace\" (5:2). The layout is 1440 wide, dark mode, Poppins, at roughly 4200 tall, with a sticky 1440x88 header (logo left, nav Home/Projects/Experience/Contact with Home in orange, \"Get In Touch\" button), a two-column hero (headline \"I do code and make content about it!\", paragraph, Get In Touch white filled plus Download CV outlined, avatar with gradient blob on the right), a full-width tech row, Projects (2 cards: image, \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\", title HTML TUTORIAL / CSS TUTORIAL, arrow), Experience (3 rows with initials mark, role, company, dates, description), and a contact footer. Palette: bg #0C0C0E, surface #141418, border #26262C, text #FFFFFF, secondary #A3A3AD, orange #D5491D, blue #1373D1. Type: display 64/72 SemiBold, h2 48/56, body 16/28, radius 8/16/24/pill. I build reusable components (Button with Style=Primary/Outline and State=Default/Hover, NavItem Default/Hover/Current, Header, TechLogo, ProjectCard, ExperienceEntry, CompanyMark variants S/MS/OC, SocialButton, Footer), then assemble the frame named exactly \"01_Home\", and add SCROLL_TO reactions on nav items to the section frames.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":25063,"input_tokens":1,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":25063}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad70c2ff-9331-4674-b010-6cfed35c5750","uuid":"804ed6fd-b9f6-473a